# Review: MessengerPlugin

The plugin matches its spec closely and is well tested. `materialize.test.ts` covers storing contacts'
messages under the verified sender, leaving non-contacts pending, acking undecodable payloads,
storing a redelivered envelope once across two devices, and converging concurrent containers.
`sender.test.ts` covers delivery and the typed errors. The `TwoUsers` and `Invitation` stories run
end to end under `ts-test-storybook`: send, tile, badge, click-to-read, and invitation Join.

The gaps are in the UI paths no test exercises: the tile menu's mark-unread and delete, the filters,
the R0 companion badge itself (the stories render their own badge from the same
`Notifications.countUnread`), and the invitation toast being shown only on the storing device. Minor
differences: `NotificationsPanel` takes the containers list rather than one `Notifications`, and
`InboxSendError` also includes `InboxAccountRequiredError`.

